\section{Supplementary formulas, illustrations and annotations}  
\subsection{Derivation of $\Delta S$ for the spin-boson framework}  

To calculate $\Delta S$, we ought to understand the expectation values $\langle \sigma_x \rangle$ and $\langle \sigma_z \rangle$ at pivotality. Adapting the findings of Anderson and Yuval \cite{Anderson:1971}, we ascertain that $\langle \sigma_z \rangle$ leaps by $\sqrt{1/\alpha}$ along the quantum crucial line $2y=-(1-\alpha)$. The expectation value of $\sigma_x$ is most readily acquired by differentiating the ground state energy: $\langle \sigma_x \rangle=-2 \, ( \partial E/\partial \Delta)$. Since the ground state energy corresponds to the free energy of the inverse-square Ising framework, we can leverage the free energy scaling relation \cite{Anderson:1971,Young:1981}

