\section*{Appendix}

Selecting an orthonormal tetrad such that $\delta\equiv(e_1 - i
e_2)/\sqrt{2}$, $D \equiv(e_3+e_4)/\sqrt{2}$ and $\Delta \equiv
(e_4-e_3)/\sqrt{2}$ ($e_4=u$ being the liquid velocity), the
components of the liquid kinematical quantities are given by the
subsequent expressions:

(expansion tensor)
\begin{eqnarray}
\theta_{12} = 0 \\
\theta_{13}+i \theta_{23} = (\alpha+\overline{\beta}+2\pi+2\overline{\tau})/\sqrt{2} \\
\theta_{11} = \theta_{22} = (\mu+\overline{\mu}-\rho-\overline{\rho})/(2\sqrt{2})\\
\theta_{33}= (\epsilon+\overline{\epsilon}-\gamma-\overline{\gamma})/\sqrt{2}
\end{eqnarray}

(acceleration vector)
\begin{eqnarray}
\dot{u}_1+ i \dot{u}_2 = -\sqrt{2}(\pi+\overline{\kappa}+2\overline{\tau})\\
\dot{u}_3 = (\epsilon+\overline{\epsilon}+\gamma+\overline{\gamma})/\sqrt{2}
\end{eqnarray}

(vorticity vector)
\begin{eqnarray}
\omega_1+i \omega_2 = \frac{i}{2} (\alpha+\overline{\beta} - 2 \overline{\tau} -2 \pi)/\sqrt{2}\\
\omega_3 = \frac{i}{2}(\rho-\overline{\rho}+\mu-\overline{\mu})/\sqrt{2}
\end{eqnarray}

