\section{Introduction}  
Consider the regular differential equation (ODE) below  
\begin{eqnarray}  
x^{\prime\prime}+g(t,x)=0,\quad t\geq0,\label{main_1}  
\end{eqnarray}  
where the nonlinearity $g$ is considered continuous everywhere. In the previous few years, numerous outcomes in the applied sciences were based on precise uniqueness outcomes for both first order and higher order ODEs addressing various scenarios outside the framework of Lipschitzian nonlinearities $g$. See, e{.}g{.}, \cite{kk,Mustafa}.  

Our aim in this note is to generalize one of the recent advancements in the theory of Nagumo uniqueness criteria \cite{nag,nag2,ath,Mejstrik}, namely the outcome from \cite{cjapan}. It has been determined that for second order ODEs, see (\ref{main_1}), if $\lim\limits_{t\searrow0}g(t,x)=0$ uniformly regarding $x\in(-1,1)$ and  
\begin{eqnarray}  
\vert g(t,x_{1})-g(t,x_{2})\vert\leq\frac{2}{t^2}\cdot\vert x_{1}-x_{2}\vert,\quad t>0,\thinspace\vert x_{1}\vert,\vert x_{2}\vert<1,\label{hyp_gen_0}  
\end{eqnarray}  
the sole solution of the equation starting with $x(0)=x^{\prime}(0)=0$ is the trivial one. This has been concluded in \cite{wintner} and further generalized in \cite{c97}. The latter paper presents a Nagumo-like criterion for $n$--th order ODEs when the coefficient $\frac{2}{t^2}$ from (\ref{hyp_gen_0}) is substituted by the Athanassov-like term $\frac{u^{\prime\prime}(t)}{u(t)}$ for some smooth function $u:[0,1]\rightarrow[0,+\infty)$ with $u(0)=0$ and $u(t)$, $u^{\prime}(t)>0$ everywhere in (0,1].

