Our objective in this note is to generalize one of the recent advancements in the theory of Nagumo uniqueness criteria \cite{nag,nag2,ath,Mejstrik}, namely the finding from \cite{cjapan}. It has been established that for second order ODEs, see (\ref{main_1}), if $\lim\limits_{t\searrow0}k(t,x)=0$ uniformly concerning $x\in(-1,1)$ and  
\begin{eqnarray}  
\vert k(t,x_{1})-k(t,x_{2})\vert\leq\frac{2}{t^2}\cdot\vert x_{1}-x_{2}\vert,\quad t>0,\thinspace\vert x_{1}\vert,\vert x_{2}\vert<1,\label{hyp_gen_0}  
\end{eqnarray}  
the unique solution of the equation starting with $x(0)=x^{\prime}(0)=0$ is the trivial one. This has been concluded in \cite{wintner} and further broadened in \cite{c97}. The latter paper presents a Nagumo-like criterion for $n$--th order ODEs when the coefficient $\frac{2}{t^2}$ from (\ref{hyp_gen_0}) is changed by the Athanassov-like term $\frac{u^{\prime\prime}(t)}{u(t)}$ for some smooth function $u:[0,1]\rightarrow[0,+\infty)$ with $u(0)=0$ and $u(t)$, $u^{\prime}(t)>0$ everywhere in (0,1].

