\section{EPAPS supplementary material}

Here we articulate and elucidate some technical facets of the calculation, presented in the main text.
The Jordan-Wigner transformation expresses as \cite{giamarchi}
\begin{gather}
S_l^+=\exp\left(i\pi\sum_{m<l}n_m\right)c_l^+,\hspace*{3mm} S_l^-=\exp\left(i\pi\sum_{m<l}n_m\right)c_l, \hspace*{3mm} S_l^z=n_l-\frac{1}{2},\hspace*{3mm}n_l=c_l^+c_l
\end{gather}
 where the $c$'s are fermionic operators.

